# tokens
LineComment   "// The builtin range type: a half-open integer sequence, constructed with"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// range(start, end) — the values start, start+1, ..., end-1 (an end at or below"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// start is the empty range). It is constructed by the two-argument form the way"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// error(\"msg\") is by the one-argument form: a native conversion that builds the"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// value. range impls foldable<int, int>, so it iterates with for and carries the"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// whole provided method set (count, any, all, map, filter, keys, values) for"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// free — its key is the 0-based position (like a list's index) and its value is"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// the element, so for...of binds the element and for...in binds the position."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// for over a range with \"of\" sums its elements: range(0, 10) is 0..9, so the"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// let total the body reassigns folds to 0 + 1 + ... + 9 = 45. This is the"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// headline example — a counted loop, written without materializing a list."
Newline       "\n"
